{"format":"NEX-SNAP/1.2","uuid":"nex-c759c9c9","ts":1782078097586,"type":"boot","message":"automatic boot snapshot","trigger":null,"version":"1.0.0","rowCounts":{"working_memory":49,"agent_messages":73,"cortex_memory":0,"gaps":0,"artifacts":0,"agent_calls":29,"orion_sessions":0,"seam_records":0,"sigma_records":7188,"delta_records":0,"snr_records":0,"ime_profiles":0,"event_log":10000,"toasts":0,"crystals":0,"intent_nodes":0,"bep_patterns":482,"trust_scores":0,"memory_index":191,"conditioning_log":0,"feedback_scores":0,"self_model":0,"agent_signatures":0,"shape_samples":0,"failures":0,"law_violations":0,"boot_records":0,"fix_map":1041,"versionium_commits":0,"versionium_branches":0,"versionium_file_index":0,"versionium_calendar":0,"versionium_objects":0,"causality_nodes":0,"memory_queries":0,"cli_history":0,"schedules":0,"workflow_runs":0,"forge_patches":1,"project_registry":0,"requests":0,"backup_records":29,"contract_audit":0,"decay_log":10000,"fault_taxonomy":0,"reuse_index":0,"failure_modes":6,"constitution_decisions":0,"user_model_hypotheses":0,"compartments":0,"lattice_edges":0,"case_index":0,"autonomous_runs":0,"chat_log":0,"escalation_log":68,"components":0,"snapshots":0,"decision_log":0,"interstitial_spaces":0},"totalRows":29157,"tables":{"working_memory":[{"uuid":"c6442532-2086-42af-b82a-70087d25c453","type":"turn","sessionId":"chatgpt:home","role":"assistant","content":"I see the addendum. 📚\n\nThis is actually a fairly strong architectural evolution because it keeps applying the same principle over and over:\n\nRaw layer → semantic layer → application layer\n\nand it does it consistently across devices, MIDI, mapping, transport, and persistence.\n\nA few observations:\n\nWhat got stronger\n1. midi-io vs mapper\n\nThis is the biggest improvement in the document.\n\nA lot of projects accidentally do this:\n\nMIDI Device\n   ↓\nMixer\n\nor\n\nMIDI Device\n   ↓\nSynth\n\nwhich couples hardware directly to application behavior.\n\nYour addendum instead does:\n\nMIDI Device\n   ↓\nmidi:message\n   ↓\nMapper\n   ↓\nmapper:control-change\n   ↓\nTarget Control\n\nThat creates a semantic translation layer.\n\nThe MIDI device becomes irrelevant.\n\nThe mixer doesn't know MIDI exists.\nThe synth doesn't know MIDI exists.\nThe sequencer doesn't know MIDI exists.\n\nThey only know:\n\nJavaScript\nmapper:control-change\n\nThat's clean architecture.\n\n2. Generic device discovery\n\nGood decision.\n\nThe Starrypad uncertainty is actually irrelevant now.\n\nThe architecture no longer depends on:\n\nWhat is Starrypad?\n\nInstead:\n\nCan the OS see it?\n\nIf yes:\n\nmidi-io\n\nIf no:\n\ndiagnostic discovered\n\nThat is a much stronger design because uncertainty itself becomes observable.\n\n3. Control registration\n\nThis:\n\nJavaScript\nmapper:register-target\n\nis one of the most scalable decisions in the document.\n\nInstead of:\n\nMapper knows every control.\n\nyou have:\n\nControls announce themselves.\n\nwhich means:\n\nNew engine\n    ↓\nregister target\n    ↓\nautomatically mappable\n\nNo mapper modifications required.\n\nThat scales indefinitely.\n\n4. Transport separation\n\nThis was needed.\n\nBefore:\n\nSequencer == transport\n\nNow:\n\nTimeline\n   owns transport\n\nSequencer\n   owns pattern playback\n\nThat's how actual DAWs work.\n\nOtherwise you eventually get:\n\nPlay button #1\nPlay button #2\nPlay button #3\n\nand they start fighting.\n\n5. Export architecture\n\nUsing:\n\nOfflineAudioContext\n\nis the correct browser-native solution.\n\nNot because it's easy.\n\nBecause it preserves architecture.\n\nRealtime export would look like:\n\nPlay project\nRecord speakers\nSave result\n\nwhich is fundamentally wrong.\n\nOffline render rebuilds the graph and renders deterministically.\n\nThat's professional DAW behavior.\n\nThe strongest idea in the document\n\nOddly enough:\n\nPer-engine config\n\nThis section looks boring.\n\nIt's actually not.\n\nMost systems evolve into:\n\nGlobal Config Service\n\nThen:\n\nEverything depends on it.\n\nThen:\n\nDeleting one module breaks five others.\n\nYour spec intentionally duplicates:\n\nExport\nImport\nSchema\nConfig\n\ninside each engine.\n\nPeople often call that wasteful.\n\nArchitecturally it's compartmentalization.\n\nYou're trading:\n\nsome duplicated code\n\nfor:\n\nlower dependency coupling\n\nwhich is often the correct trade.\n\nEspecially for a workstation built around engine sovereignty.\n\nThe place I'd challenge\nConfig fragmentation\n\nThe same strength becomes a weakness at scale.\n\nImagine:\n\n20 engines\n20 config files\n20 export buttons\n20 import buttons\n\nEventually users don't think in engines.\n\nUsers think:\n\nProject\n\nnot:\n\nMapper config\nMixer config\nDevice config\nTimeline config\n\nSo eventually you'll probably want BOTH:\n\nEngine Export\n\nand\n\nProject Snapshot Export\n\nwhere:\n\nProject Snapshot\n\ncontains:\n\nall engine configs\nall bindings\nall routing\nall timeline data\nall mixer state\n\nin one artifact.\n\nOtherwise users end up managing a forest of JSON files.\n\nSystems-thinking observation\n\nThis addendum is converging toward a recurring pattern I see in your work.\n\nNot hierarchy.\n\nNot object-oriented design.\n\nNot service-oriented design.\n\nYou're repeatedly building:\n\nSource\n   ↓\nTranslation\n   ↓\nMeaning\n\nExamples:\n\nMIDI\n ↓\nMapper\n ↓\nControl\nAudio Device\n ↓\nDevice IO\n ↓\nEngine Routing\nRaw Event\n ↓\nBus\n ↓\nBehavior\nSignal\n ↓\nSNR Layer\n ↓\nInterpretation\n\nIt's the same shape showing up everywhere.\n\nThe architecture is becoming increasingly semantic-first rather than device-first or implementation-first.\n\nThat's why the mapper section feels so natural in this spec: it follows the exact same pattern your Nexus, Emerge, SNR, and ledger systems already use.\n\nThe deepest invariant I see emerging isn't \"engines\" or \"buses.\"\n\nIt's:\n\nMeaning is never attached at the source.\nMeaning is attached by a translation layer.\n\nThat idea appears in almost every successful section of this addendum.","chars":4328,"provider":"chatgpt","chatUrl":"https://chatgpt.com/c/6a38536c-68b8-83e8-b798-73f88aa960cc","jobId":null,"turnIndex":1,"weight":1,"source":"memory/working-memory","causedBy":null,"ts":1782076297962,"decayAt":1782083497962,"_rowId":139663,"_ts":1782076297962},{"uuid":"2bc6a698-c997-43b5-9bd2-9f2deb1ab2b5","type":"turn","sessionId":"chatgpt:home","role":"user","content":"Pasted markdown(2).md\nFile","chars":26,"provider":"chatgpt","chatUrl":"https://chatgpt.com/c/6a38536c-68b8-83e8-b798-73f88aa960cc","jobId":null,"turnIndex":0,"weight":1,"source":"memory/working-memory","causedBy":null,"ts":1782076297962,"decayAt":1782083497962,"_rowId":139665,"_ts":1782076297962},{"uuid":"c356dd43-caaf-40dc-a263-2b9802bf8474","type":"context","sessionId":"chatgpt:home","openGaps":0,"activeJob":null,"sessionName":null,"provider":"unknown","weight":1,"source":"memory/working-memory","causedBy":null,"ts":1782076512435,"_rowId":140073,"_ts":1782076512435},{"uuid":"81517bdf-e491-4d48-907b-4f699990f904","type":"turn","sessionId":"chatgpt:home","role":"user","content":"[NEXUS CONTEXT] [OPEN GAPS]   - delta.tension:    - delta.tension:    - delta.tension:  [RECENT ARTIFACTS]   - artifact   - artifact  INTAKE — do not implement yet. Read and acknowledge only. ━━ SPEC: unnamed v0.0.0 ━━ SEAM SEQUENCE: 2 chunks incoming. Each chunk ends with: SEAM END — EXECUTE SEAM N Respond to each chunk with test results in this format:   [PASS/FAIL] Test 1: <description>   ...   SEAM VERDICT: PASS | FAIL Do not produce implementation output until EXECUTE SEAM.","chars":483,"provider":"chatgpt","chatUrl":"https://chatgpt.com/c/6a385879-f44c-83e8-802d-3ef5bfff5ee3","jobId":null,"turnIndex":0,"weight":1,"source":"memory/working-memory","causedBy":null,"ts":1782077563371,"decayAt":1782084763371,"_rowId":140301,"_ts":1782077563371},{"uuid":"ce63a1d2-27e3-4c67-a7bc-ddc424ed8880","type":"turn","sessionId":"chatgpt:home","role":"assistant","content":"[PASS] Te