ype":"raid.health","payload":"{\"ollama\":{\"online\":true,\"fails\":0},\"guardian-claude\":{\"online\":true,\"fails\":0},\"guardian-chatgpt\":{\"online\":true,\"fails\":0},\"claude\":{\"online\":true,\"fails\":0},\"chatgpt\":{\"online\":true,\"fails\":0},\"gemini\":{\"online\":true,\"fails\":0},\"perplexity\":{\"online\":true,\"fails\":0}}","source":"raid","ts":1782076290131,"_rowId":139649,"_ts":1782076290131},{"uuid":"388eb39f-859e-4bf5-b325-61e89dd1508b","type":"raid.health","payload":"{\"ollama\":{\"online\":true,\"fails\":0},\"guardian-claude\":{\"online\":true,\"fails\":0},\"guardian-chatgpt\":{\"online\":true,\"fails\":0},\"claude\":{\"online\":true,\"fails\":0},\"chatgpt\":{\"online\":true,\"fails\":0},\"gemini\":{\"online\":true,\"fails\":0},\"perplexity\":{\"online\":true,\"fails\":0}}","source":"raid","ts":1782076290131,"_rowId":139650,"_ts":1782076290131},{"uuid":"2ef24f49-b1a2-44a8-b40a-872f9f1c8c3b","type":"gap-loop.ecology","payload":{"total":1,"by_type":{"TEMPORAL":1},"by_status":{"needs_manual":1},"critical_count":0,"temporal_accumulation":false,"causal_unresolved":0,"ecology_health":"nominal"},"source":"gap-loop","causedBy":null,"ts":1782076292829,"_rowId":139655,"_ts":1782076292829},{"uuid":"12c61132-fcac-42f8-8838-3d5cde38aeea","type":"heartbeat.tick","payload":{"orchestrator":{"online":true,"latencyMs":11},"cortex":{"online":true,"latencyMs":7},"guardian":{"online":true,"latencyMs":0},"idearium":{"online":true,"latencyMs":1},"bridge":{"online":true,"latencyMs":1},"architect":{"online":true,"latencyMs":0},"emerge":{"online":false,"latencyMs":0},"diagnostic":{"online":true,"latencyMs":1}},"source":"heartbeat","causedBy":null,"ts":1782076292905,"_rowId":139658,"_ts":1782076292926},{"uuid":"a6b1e148-25d3-4f4a-865c-e3774f5f3872","type":"working.memory.turn","payload":{"type":"turn","sessionId":"chatgpt:home","role":"assistant","content":"I see the addendum. 📚\n\nThis is actually a fairly strong architectural evolution because it keeps applying the same principle over and over:\n\nRaw layer → semantic layer → application layer\n\nand it does it consistently across devices, MIDI, mapping, transport, and persistence.\n\nA few observations:\n\nWhat got stronger\n1. midi-io vs mapper\n\nThis is the biggest improvement in the document.\n\nA lot of projects accidentally do this:\n\nMIDI Device\n   ↓\nMixer\n\nor\n\nMIDI Device\n   ↓\nSynth\n\nwhich couples hardware directly to application behavior.\n\nYour addendum instead does:\n\nMIDI Device\n   ↓\nmidi:message\n   ↓\nMapper\n   ↓\nmapper:control-change\n   ↓\nTarget Control\n\nThat creates a semantic translation layer.\n\nThe MIDI device becomes irrelevant.\n\nThe mixer doesn't know MIDI exists.\nThe synth doesn't know MIDI exists.\nThe sequencer doesn't know MIDI exists.\n\nThey only know:\n\nJavaScript\nmapper:control-change\n\nThat's clean architecture.\n\n2. Generic device discovery\n\nGood decision.\n\nThe Starrypad uncertainty is actually irrelevant now.\n\nThe architecture no longer depends on:\n\nWhat is Starrypad?\n\nInstead:\n\nCan the OS see it?\n\nIf yes:\n\nmidi-io\n\nIf no:\n\ndiagnostic discovered\n\nThat is a much stronger design because uncertainty itself becomes observable.\n\n3. Control registration\n\nThis:\n\nJavaScript\nmapper:register-target\n\nis one of the most scalable decisions in the document.\n\nInstead of:\n\nMapper knows every control.\n\nyou have:\n\nControls announce themselves.\n\nwhich means:\n\nNew engine\n    ↓\nregister target\n    ↓\nautomatically mappable\n\nNo mapper modifications required.\n\nThat scales indefinitely.\n\n4. Transport separation\n\nThis was needed.\n\nBefore:\n\nSequencer == transport\n\nNow:\n\nTimeline\n   owns transport\n\nSequencer\n   owns pattern playback\n\nThat's how actual DAWs work.\n\nOtherwise you eventually get:\n\nPlay button #1\nPlay button #2\nPlay button #3\n\nand they start fighting.\n\n5. Export architecture\n\nUsing:\n\nOfflineAudioContext\n\nis the correct browser-native solution.\n\nNot because it's easy.\n\nBecause it preserves architecture.\n\nRealtime export would look like:\n\nPlay project\nRecord speakers\nSave result\n\nwhich is fundamentally wrong.\n\nOffline render rebuilds the graph and renders deterministically.\n\nThat's professional DAW behavior.\n\nThe strongest idea in the document\n\nOddly enough:\n\nPer-engine config\n\nThis section looks boring.\n\nIt's actually not.\n\nMost systems evolve into:\n\nGlobal Config Service\n\nThen:\n\nEverything depends on it.\n\nThen:\n\nDeleting one module breaks five others.\n\nYour spec intentionally duplicates:\n\nExport\nImport\nSchema\nConfig\n\ninside each engine.\n\nPeople often call that wasteful.\n\nArchitecturally it's compartmentalization.\n\nYou're trading:\n\nsome duplicated code\n\nfor:\n\nlower dependency coupling\n\nwhich is often the correct trade.\n\nEspecially for a workstation built around engine sovereignty.\n\nThe place I'd challenge\nConfig fragmentation\n\nThe same strength becomes a weakness at scale.\n\nImagine:\n\n20 engines\n20 config files\n20 export buttons\n20 import buttons\n\nEventually users don't think in engines.\n\nUsers think:\n\nProject\n\nnot:\n\nMapper config\nMixer config\nDevice config\nTimeline config\n\nSo eventually you'll probably want BOTH:\n\nEngine Export\n\nand\n\nProject Snapshot Export\n\nwhere:\n\nProject Snapshot\n\ncontains:\n\nall engine configs\nall bindings\nall routing\nall timeline data\nall mixer state\n\nin one artifact.\n\nOtherwise users end up managing a forest of JSON files.\n\nSystems-thinking observation\n\nThis addendum is converging toward a recurring pattern I see in your work.\n\nNot hierarchy.\n\nNot object-oriented design.\n\nNot service-oriented design.\n\nYou're repeatedly building:\n\nSource\n   ↓\nTranslation\n   ↓\nMeaning\n\nExamples:\n\nMIDI\n ↓\nMapper\n ↓\nControl\nAudio Device\n ↓\nDevice IO\n ↓\nEngine Routing\nRaw Event\n ↓\nBus\n ↓\nBehavior\nSignal\n ↓\nSNR Layer\n ↓\nInterpretation\n\nIt's the same shape showing up everywhere.\n\nThe architecture is becoming increasingly semantic-first rather than device-first or implementation-first.\n\nThat's why the mapper section feels so natural in this spec: it follows the exact same pattern your Nexus, Emerge, SNR, and ledger systems already use.\n\nThe deepest invariant I see emerging isn't \"engines\" or \"buses.\"\n\nIt's:\n\nMeaning is never attached at the source.\nMeaning is attached by a translation layer.\n\nThat idea appears in almost every successful section of this addendum.","provider":"chatgpt","chatUrl":"https://chatgpt.com/c/6a38536c-68b8-83e8-b798-73f88aa960cc","turnIndex":1,"ts":1782076293558,"_provider":"chatgpt","_chatUrl":"https://chatgpt.com/c/6a38536c-68b8-83e8-b798-73f88aa960cc"},"source":"userscript-memory","causedBy":null,"ts":1782076297962,"_rowId":139664,"_ts":1782076297962},{"uuid":"c873d4b0-4c7f-4d4b-a7ad-066072528e79","type":"working.memory.turn","payload":{"type":"turn","sessionId":"chatgpt:home","role":"user","content":"Pasted markdown(2).md\nFile","provider":"chatgpt","chatUrl":"https://chatgpt.com/c/6a38536c-68b8-83e8-b798-73f88aa960cc","turnIndex":0,"ts":1782076273955,"_provider":"chatgpt","_chatUrl":"https://chatgpt.com/c/6a38536c-68b8-83e8-b798-73f88aa960cc"},"source":"userscript-memory","causedBy":null,"ts":1782076297962,"_rowId":139666,"_ts":1782076297962},{"uuid":"c75f91ac-cd1a-4f3a-9c62-8b692042c236","type":"raid.health","payload":"{\"ollama\":{\"online\":true,\"fails\":0},\"guardian-claude\":{\"online\":true,\"fails\":0},\"guardian-chatgpt\":{\"online\":true,\"fails\":0},\"claude\":{\"online\":true,\"fails\":0},\"chatgpt\":{\"online\":true,\"fails\":0},\"gemini\":{\"online\":true,\"fails\":0},\"perplexity\":{\"online\":true,\"fails\":0}}","source":"raid","ts":1782076300138,"_rowId":139670,"_ts":1782076300138},{"uuid":"b6772e92-887b-4285-a95a-a84417e49a66","type":"raid.health","payload":"{\"ollama\":{\"online\":true,\"fails\":0},\"guardian-claude\":{\"online\":true,\"fails\":0},\"guardian-chatgpt\":{\"online\":true,\"fails\":0},\"claude\":{\"online\":true,\"fails\":0},\"chatgpt\":{\"online\":true,\"fails\":0},\"gemini\":{\"online\":true,\"fails\":0},\"perplexity\":{\"online\":true,\"fails\":0}}","source":"raid","ts":1782076300138,"_rowId":139671,"_ts":1782076300138},{"uuid":"bb6803c9-a0c5-4876-b66f-6a590dff4a13","type":"intelligence.cross_ledger_analysis","payload":{"windowMs":300000,"sigmaEvents":59,"avgSigma":0,"maxSigma":0,"highSigmaCount":0,"avgFriction":0,"avgTension":0,"openGapsTotal":0,"recentGaps":0,"driftScore":0,"driftLevel":"normal","patterns":81},"source":"cortex/intelligence","causedBy":null,"ts":1782076303083,"_rowId":139677,"_ts":1782076303083},{"uuid":"e26a501c-7375-48ed-a52b-45830d25896a","type":"intelligence.failure_scan","payload":{"failureSources":0,"faultClasses":0,"topFaults":[]},"source":"cortex/intelligence","causedBy":null,"ts":1782076304986,"_rowId":139681,"_ts":1782076304987},{"uuid":"56bc23d9-d52b-4f49-abff-f8d7a9f2233e","type":"gap-loop.ecology","payload":{"total":1,"by_type":{"TEMPORAL":1},"by_status":{"needs_manual":1},"critical_count":0,"temporal_accumulation":false,"causal_unresolved":0,"ecology_health":"nominal"},"source":"gap-loop","causedBy":null,"ts":1782076307831,"_rowId":139685,"_ts":1782076307832},{"uuid":"03cbc876-8f2d-48b0-bfd7-7ea5abaa0432","type":"heartbeat.tick","payload":{"orchestrator":{"online":true,"latencyMs":11},"cortex":{"online":true,"latencyMs":8},"guardian":{"online":true,"latencyMs":1},"idearium":{"online":true,"latencyMs":0},"bridge":{"online":true,"latencyMs":1},"architect":{"online":true,"latencyMs":0},"emerge":{"online":false,"latencyMs":1},"diagnostic":{"online":true,"latencyMs":0}},"source":"heartbeat","causedBy":null,"ts":1782076307913,"_rowId":139686,"_ts":1782076307935},{"uuid":"8a209ef4-7e32-4758-9a5e-3b014b40b7a7","type":"heartbeat.pulse","payload":{"orchestrator":{"status":{"ok":true,"latencyMs":16,"ts":1782076309903},"trust":{"ok":true,"latencyMs":1,"ts":1782076309903}},"cortex":{"e